From: CarPlay C0 lane (2026-11-23)
Subject: 0632 sweet_nub: second late sample of the channel fields (raw, never dereferenced)

The 5 s sample runs before Apple's NCM data client starts (it attaches around 30 s), so the raw
ctl+0x110/0x120 values we print there are the pre-client state (25 s boot showed the packed
0x5ac00000000). Add one 20 s tsleep after the fallback branch and print started/children plus the
two fields raw again, so C1's endpoint-dispatch step can see whether those fields become real
objects once the data client is up. No dereference is added (0528's rule).
--- a/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
@@ -652,6 +652,19 @@
 		printf("SWEET NUB: nothing matched; pass sweet_nub=3 (or 4) to call createUSBDevice "
 		    "from here\n");
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * 0632: second sample, after Apple's NCM data client has had time to start (~30 s). The two
+	 * channel fields are printed raw again -- still no dereference -- so the next C1 step learns
+	 * whether they are packed values or real objects by then. Costs one tsleep.
+	 */
+	(void)tsleep(&sweet_nub_wait, PZERO, "sweetnub3", 20 * hz);
+	printf("SWEET NUB: late sample: started %d, children %d\n",
+	    ctl->isInactive() ? 0 : 1, children);
+	for (unsigned off = 0x110; off <= 0x120; off += 0x10) {
+		printf("SWEET NUB: late ctl+0x%x = %p (raw, not dereferenced)\n", off,
+		    *(void **)((char *)ctl + off));
+	}
 }
 
 #endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET */
